+## 4. [HIGH] The in-browser npm installer is a security boundary, not a convenience feature
+
+**Impact.** Tar entry paths, symlinks/hardlinks, oversized files, decompression ratios, package integrity, redirects, and lifecycle scripts are attacker-controlled. A single normalization mismatch can write outside node_modules or consume the tab.
+
+**Recommended change.** Validate every archive entry after POSIX normalization; reject absolute paths, .., device nodes and escaping links; cap entries/expanded bytes/ratio; verify lockfile or registry integrity before extraction; default lifecycle scripts off and capability-gate them.
+
+**Evidence.**
