+## 5. [HIGH] Service Worker routing and multi-instance ownership need explicit lifecycle semantics
+
+**Impact.** A service worker is shared by scope and outlives tabs. Multiple Nacelle instances, version upgrades, stale clients, and route-name collisions can cross-wire preview traffic or leave old workers serving new runtimes.
+
+**Recommended change.** Namespace routes by unguessable runtime/session ID, bind them to a specific client, require leases/heartbeats, unregister stale routes, version the wire protocol, and test two tabs running different Nacelle versions.
+
